Falsifies `extensible_host_controller_interface::verification::every_command_trb_puts_its_slot_endpoint_and_pointer_in_their_fields`.

The defect: `reset_endpoint` puts the device context index one bit high, at 17 to 21, so the controller reads twice the endpoint asked for and index 16 and above spill into the reserved bit 21.

Expected to fail: the harness's check that the Reset Endpoint TRB's dword 3 holds the endpoint at bits 16 to 20 and nothing outside its type, slot and endpoint fields.

diff --git a/src/transfer_request_block.rs b/src/transfer_request_block.rs
--- a/src/transfer_request_block.rs
+++ b/src/transfer_request_block.rs
@@ -266,7 +266,7 @@ impl TransferRequestBlock {
             0,
             0,
             control(transfer_request_block_type::RESET_ENDPOINT)
-                | (device_context_index.get() as u32) << 16
+                | (device_context_index.get() as u32) << 17
                 | (slot.get() as u32) << 24,
         ])
     }
